** Their raise of a weak two-bid

The raise is preemptive, so the direct seat needs an opening hand to act at
the three level: a takeout double (13--17 and short, or any 18+), a five-card
major, a six-card minor at the four level, 3NT with 16--19 and a stopper.
In the balancing seat the same calls with 11+.

#CUT raised-weak-two
3N = {prio:3} 16--19 hcp, stopper
  #STOP
c\O = {prio:2} 13--17 hcp, 5+!\o
  #STOP
cm = {prio:2} 13--17 hcp, 6+m
  #STOP
D = {prio:1} 13--17 hcp and 0--2!\t or 18+ hcp
  #STOP
#STOP
#ENDCUT

#CUT raised-weak-two-balancing
c\O = {prio:2} 11--16 hcp, 5+!\o
  #STOP
cm = {prio:2} 11--16 hcp, 6+m
  #STOP
D = {prio:1} 11--16 hcp and 0--2!\t or 17+ hcp
  #STOP
#STOP
#ENDCUT

