** Opener when the opponents come in after responder has passed (P12 batch 2)

Responder's pass of the opening showed 0--5 hcp. When the fourth hand then
balances, opener passes a minimum balanced hand; he rebids a six-card suit at
the cheapest level, bids a second five-card suit, and with 16+ and shortness
in their suit doubles for takeout. Responder answers that double as any
takeout double: an unbid four-card major or minor at the cheapest level, three
cards of opener's suit, or a pass with five cards in theirs. Over their
balancing 1NT opener's double (16+) is for penalty.

#CUT opener-after-their-balance
c\S = {prio:2} 12--17 hcp, 6+\S
  #STOP
cM = {prio:3} 12--17 hcp, 5+\S, 5+M
  #STOP
cm = {prio:3} 12--17 hcp, 5+\S, 5+m
  #STOP
#STOP
#ENDCUT

#CUT answer-opener-takeout-double
P = {prio:4} 5+\T
  #STOP
cM = {prio:3} 4+M
  #STOP
cm = {prio:2} 4+m
  #STOP
c\S = {prio:1} 3+\S
  #STOP
#STOP
#ENDCUT

1X-(P)-P-(D)-
#PASTE opener-after-their-balance \S=X

1X-(P)-P-(1N)-
D = {prio:1} 16+ hcp
  #STOP
#PASTE opener-after-their-balance \S=X

1X-(P)-P-(1Y)-
D = {prio:1} 16+ hcp, 0--1Y
#PASTE opener-after-their-balance \S=X

1X-(P)-P-(1Y)-D-(P)-
#PASTE answer-opener-takeout-double \S=X \T=Y

1X-(P)-P-(2Y)-
D = {prio:1} 16+ hcp, 0--1Y
#PASTE opener-after-their-balance \S=X

1X-(P)-P-(2Y)-D-(P)-
