** Opener when they bid again after an overcall (P12 batch 2)

The booklet's competitive principle (bid what you have, and do not bid
twice with the same values) applied to opener's second turn: over their
advance, when responder has passed or doubled, opener rebids a six-card suit
at the cheapest level and shows a second five-card suit; after responder's
negative double he bids a four-card unbid major the double promised
(at the three or four level only with 14+). Otherwise he passes.

#CUT opener-competes
c\S = {prio:2} 12--16 hcp, 6+\S
  #STOP
cM = {prio:3} 12--16 hcp, 5+\S, 5+M
  #STOP
cm = {prio:3} 12--16 hcp, 5+\S, 5+m
  #STOP
#STOP
#ENDCUT

